  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice, built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon of the Adriatic Sea, has always been a unique and fascinating place. Its history dates back to the 5th century when it was founded by refugees fleeing from the barbarian invasions of the mainland. Over time, the city developed into a major trading centre, attracting merchants and artisans from all over Europe.\n\nThe architecture of Venice is also notable for its use of water as a building material. The famous St Mark's Square, with its imposing basilica and campanile, was built on top of an ancient pagan temple dedicated to the goddess Astarte. The square is surrounded by elaborate Gothic palaces that were once the residences of wealthy merchants.\n\nDespite its beauty and historical significance, Venice has faced numerous challenges over the centuries. In the 18th century, it suffered a devastating plague that killed nearly half of its population. More recently, the city has struggled with the effects of mass tourism, which have put pressure on its infrastructure and environment.\n\nHowever, in recent years, the Venetian authorities have taken steps to address these issues. They have implemented measures to reduce the number of tourists and to promote sustainable tourism practices. The city's residents are also working together to preserve their unique cultural heritage and to protect the environment.\n\nAs a result, Venice is once again becoming a vibrant and thriving city, where art, history, and culture come alive. Visitors from all over the world can experience its beauty and magic by wandering through its narrow streets and canals, taking in the stunning architecture and admiring the works of art that adorn its buildings.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason why refugees founded Venice in the 5th century?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To escape from war\", \"To find a new place to trade\", \"To flee from barbarian invasions on the mainland\", \"To establish a new Christian kingdom\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To flee from barbarian invasions on the mainland\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is notable about the architecture of Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It uses only stone and brick\", \"It incorporates water as a building material\", \"It features only Gothic palaces\", \"It has no notable examples of ancient buildings\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It incorporates water as a building material\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and negative\", \"Indifferent and neutral\", \"Positive and enthusiastic\", \"Somewhat pessimistic but ultimately hopeful\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Somewhat pessimistic but ultimately hopeful\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the effect of mass tourism on Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It has no significant impact\", \"It promotes cultural exchange and economic growth\", \"It puts pressure on its infrastructure and environment\", \"It attracts new investment and jobs\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It puts pressure on its infrastructure and environment\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's purpose in writing this text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To inform readers about Venice's history\", \"To persuade readers to visit Venice\", \"To describe the city's architecture and cultural heritage\", \"To raise awareness about the challenges facing Venice\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To raise awareness about the challenges facing Venice\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
